  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At the Mourillon beaches site, the City of Toulon has set up a dog park: a space dedicated to dogs, with two clearly separate areas, one for small animals, the other for the largest dogs (City of Toulon).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>In the documents we read, the City of Toulon gives no details on the dog park's hours or maximum length of stay: ask on-site. On the rest of the Mourillon beaches, the city states that dogs, even on a leash, are banned from the lawns and the sand; they are allowed on a leash only on the Henri-Fabre promenade (the tourist office specifies: from 1 September to 31 May, and from 1 June to 31 August only between 6am and 8.30am).</p>
      <p>This dog park is one of the canine spaces in the Mourillon area, not to be confused with the two nearby dog beaches: Anse Tabarly (swimming area for dogs) and Pipady beach at the foot of the Tour Royale (a fenced 2,000 m² beach, opened in 2026). The dog park itself is not a swimming spot — it's a land-based space dedicated to dogs.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Mourillon area has several distinct canine spaces (dog park, Anse Tabarly for swimming, Pipady beach); check which one matches what you're looking for.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The four sandy coves of the Mourillon beaches, Anse Tabarly and Pipady beach are all a few minutes' walk away, as are Fort Saint-Louis and the Mourillon acclimatisation garden.</p>
